@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
    <h1>A polished front end on a simple MVC foundation.</h1>
    <p>Fieldnotes is a portfolio-ready ASP.NET Core project that demonstrates controller routing, Razor-rendered pages, shared layouts, static assets, and environment-aware error handling.</p>
</section>

<section class="about-grid" aria-label="Project details">
    <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h2>What works now</h2>
        <p>A responsive stories page, an About page, a real privacy statement, reusable navigation and footer, accessible focus styles, and the standard production error route.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h2>How it is built</h2>
        <p>.NET 10 and ASP.NET Core MVC handle requests and routing. Controllers select Razor views, while a shared layout and one custom stylesheet create a consistent interface.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h2>What comes next</h2>
        <p>Real post models, Entity Framework Core persistence, create/edit workflows, authentication, categories, search, comments, tests, and a public .NET deployment.</p>
    </article>
</section>
